// The generic-TYPE half. `kama check` used to say OK to exactly this shape: the emit walk reached generic
// FUNCTIONS only, so a library's public generic container could ship green with two errors in a member
// body nothing in that library instantiated. Fixed in 0.9.38–0.9.43; this fixture is what holds it fixed.
//
// It is not one loop away from the function half, which is why the note was worth keeping: handing the
// template's own `ClassInfo` to `emitClassDefinitions` failed 628 of 641 corpus fixtures, because a
// `_genericTypes` entry is a SHAPE AWAITING SPECIALIZATION — its `when` gates unevaluated, its `ctors` map
// not the one an instance gets. What turns a shape into a class is `registerGenericTypeInst`, and it needs
// real arguments; distinct synthetic ones are exactly what an opaque parameter is.
type value Holder<T> {
    T item;
    public ctor make(T x) { this.item = give x; }
    public fn void broken() {
        int32 x = "not an int";      // ERROR: a `string` cannot initialize an `int32`
        undefinedFunction(a: 1);     // ERROR: no such function, at any instantiation
    }
}
fn int32 main() { return 0; }
